@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-top-layer`

-- Tests for the "highest layer" arithmetic shared by s 91(b)(1), s 91(b1) and s 125C(b).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the bands and the cap (the arithmetic is beside each group) before it was run.
-- The scales are the ones s 121 prints in the deposited text (301,200 / 560,280 and the (b)(1) bands 84,120 / 120,720 / 228,000 / 301,200).
-- They are FIXTURES here: which scale applies to a gain is s 121's business (row IL-03), and the (b)(1) scale above 301,200 is taken
-- to continue with the bands of (a)(2) and (a)(3) (an assumption of this test file, not of the rule: the rule takes the scale as an input).

§ `Tests of the top layer`

GIVEN u IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a band ending at` u `at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS JUST u
        `rate of the band`        IS r

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a last band at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS NOTHING
        `rate of the band`        IS r

-- s 121(a): 31% to 301,200; 35% to 560,280; 47% above.
`the scale of s 121(a)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

-- s 121(b)(1) for income from personal exertion or an individual of 60: 10% to 84,120; 14% to 120,720; 20% to 228,000; 31% to 301,200,
-- then the bands of (a).
`the scale of s 121(b)(1)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 84_120 `at the rate` (10%),
         `a band ending at` 120_720 `at the rate` (14%),
         `a band ending at` 228_000 `at the rate` (20%),
         `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

`no cap` MEANS `these rates are percentages, and nothing in the scale exceeds a hundred percent`

§§ `The part of a layer in a band`
-- 100,000 to 400,000 in the band 301,200 to 560,280: 400,000 - 301,200 = 98,800.
#ASSERT `the part of the layer from` 100_000 `to` 400_000 `lying in the band from` 301_200 `up to` (JUST 560_280) EQUALS 98_800
-- The layer ends before the band starts: nought. The layer starts after the band ends: nought.
#ASSERT `the part of the layer from` 0 `to` 300_000 `lying in the band from` 301_200 `up to` (JUST 560_280) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the part of the layer from` 600_000 `to` 700_000 `lying in the band from` 301_200 `up to` (JUST 560_280) EQUALS 0
-- The last band has no top: 600,000 to 700,000 above 560,280 is all in it.
#ASSERT `the part of the layer from` 600_000 `to` 700_000 `lying in the band from` 560_280 `up to` NOTHING EQUALS 100_000

§§ `One layer, one band`
-- Other income 0, gain 100,000, scale (a), cap 25%: all in the 31% band, each shekel at min(31%, 25%) = 25%: 25,000.
-- The average reading: the lesser of 31,000 (the bands) and 25% x 100,000 = 25,000: 25,000. They agree, so the default answers.
#ASSERT `the tax on a layer of` 100_000 `standing on the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, applying the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` EQUALS 25_000
#ASSERT `the tax on a layer of` 100_000 `standing on the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, applying the cap as` `the average rate over the whole gain is capped` EQUALS 25_000
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 100_000 `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` EQUALS 25_000
-- Uncapped: 100,000 x 31% = 31,000.
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 100_000 `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `with the rate capped at` `no cap` `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` EQUALS 31_000
-- Under the cap in one band: scale (b)(1), other 0, gain 50,000 in the 10% band: 5,000 on both readings.
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 50_000 `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` EQUALS 5_000
-- Exactly the first band of (b)(1): 84,120 x 10% = 8,412.
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 84_120 `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` EQUALS 8_412
-- Two low bands, under the cap: 84,120 x 10% + 15,880 x 14% = 8,412 + 2,223.2 = 10,635.2, the same on both readings (the average is 10.6352%).
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 100_000 `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` EQUALS 10_635.2
-- A zero gain pays nothing.
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 0 `above the other taxable income` 250_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` EQUALS 0

§§ `Fork T1: a gain that stands in bands on both sides of the cap`
-- Scale (b)(1), other income 220,000, gain 100,000: the layer is 220,000 to 320,000.
--   20% band (120,720 to 228,000): 8,000 ; 31% band (228,000 to 301,200): 73,200 ; 35% band (301,200 to 560,280): 18,800.
--   each band capped at 25%: 8,000 x 20% = 1,600 ; 73,200 x 25% = 18,300 ; 18,800 x 25% = 4,700 ; total 24,600.
--   the bands uncapped: 1,600 + 73,200 x 31% (22,692) + 18,800 x 35% (6,580) = 30,872 ; the average capped: the lesser of 30,872 and 25,000 = 25,000.
#ASSERT `the tax on a layer of` 100_000 `standing on the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, applying the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` EQUALS 24_600
#ASSERT `the tax on a layer of` 100_000 `standing on the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, applying the cap as` `the average rate over the whole gain is capped` EQUALS 25_000
#ASSERT `the tax on a layer of` 100_000 `standing on the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` `no cap` `, applying the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` EQUALS 30_872
#ASSERT REFUSED `the tax on the top layer` 100_000 `above the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` BECAUSE "the way a cap on the rate applies where the gain stands in several bands is not decided by the text, and here it changes the answer"
#ASSERT `the tax on the top layer` 100_000 `above the other taxable income` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `with the rate capped at` (25%) `, reading the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` EQUALS 24_600

§§ `Three parts of one gain (fork T2)`
-- Scale (a), other income 0, parts of 100,000 each, caps none / 20% / 25%: the parts stand in 0 to 300,000, wholly in the 31% band, so
-- every order gives part 1 100,000 x 31% = 31,000 + part 2 100,000 x 20% = 20,000 + part 3 100,000 x 25% = 25,000 = 76,000.
#ASSERT `the tax of three parts, at the readings,` 100_000 `and` 100_000 `and` 100_000 `capped at` `no cap` `and` (20%) `and` (25%) `above the other taxable income` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the cap as` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `and the places of the parts as` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` EQUALS 76_000
-- Other income 250,000, parts 100,000 (no cap), 50,000 (20%), 50,000 (25%), scale (a).
--   alone: part 1 on 250,000 to 350,000: 51,200 x 31% (15,872) + 48,800 x 35% (17,080) = 32,952 ; part 2 on 250,000 to 300,000, wholly in the 31% band,
--          at 20%: 10,000 ; part 3 the same at 25%: 12,500 ; total 55,452.
--   earliest lowest: part 1 32,952 ; part 2 on 350,000 to 400,000 (35% band) at 20%: 10,000 ; part 3 on 400,000 to 450,000 at 25%: 12,500 ; total 55,452.
--   earliest highest: part 3 on 250,000 to 300,000 at 25%: 12,500 ; part 2 on 300,000 to 350,000 (1,200 at 31%, 48,800 at 35%) at 20%: 10,000
--          (each band capped: 1,200 x 20% + 48,800 x 20%; the average: the lesser of 17,452 and 10,000) ; part 1 on 350,000 to 450,000 at 35%: 35,000 ; total 57,500.
#ASSERT `the tax of three parts` 100_000 `and` 50_000 `and` 50_000 `capped at` `no cap` `and` (20%) `and` (25%) `above the other taxable income` 250_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, applying the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` `, with the parts placed as` `each part stands alone on top of the other income` EQUALS 55_452
#ASSERT `the tax of three parts` 100_000 `and` 50_000 `and` 50_000 `capped at` `no cap` `and` (20%) `and` (25%) `above the other taxable income` 250_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, applying the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` `, with the parts placed as` `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period lowest` EQUALS 55_452
#ASSERT `the tax of three parts` 100_000 `and` 50_000 `and` 50_000 `capped at` `no cap` `and` (20%) `and` (25%) `above the other taxable income` 250_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, applying the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` `, with the parts placed as` `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest` EQUALS 57_500
#ASSERT REFUSED `the tax of three parts, at the readings,` 100_000 `and` 50_000 `and` 50_000 `capped at` `no cap` `and` (20%) `and` (25%) `above the other taxable income` 250_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` `and the places of the parts as` `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` BECAUSE "the place of each part of a gain within the top layer is not decided by the text, and here it changes the answer"
#ASSERT `the tax of three parts, at the readings,` 100_000 `and` 50_000 `and` 50_000 `capped at` `no cap` `and` (20%) `and` (25%) `above the other taxable income` 250_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the cap as` `the rate of each band is capped` `and the places of the parts as` `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest` EQUALS 57_500
